 r←{packageID}GetPackageList_ parms;list;list2;list3;uniqueIDs;data;majors;names
⍝ Returns one row per package: [;1] name, [;2] number of major versions, [;3] description,
⍝ [;4] project URL, [;5] operating systems, [;6] 'Yes' for a user command, [;7] tags and
⍝ [;8] the latest major version, like 'aplteam-Cider-0'.
 r←0 8⍴''
 packageID←{0<⎕NC ⍵:⍎⍵ ⋄ ''}'packageID'
 list←Reg.GetAllPackages G.RegistryPath
 list←G.RegistryPath Reg.RemoveDeprecatedPackages list
 list2←list Reg.ListPackages(G.RegistryPath,packageID)parms
 list3←Reg.RemoveVersionNumber¨list
 :If 0<≢uniqueIDs←(⌽,list){⍺[(Reg.RemoveVersionNumber¨⍺)⍳⍵]}list2[;1]     ⍝ ⌽ them in order to get the latest version
     data←↑Reg.FetchAdditionalDataForListPackages¨G.RegistryPath∘,¨uniqueIDs
     data[;4]←'[,;]'⎕R', '⊣data[;4]  ⍝ Replace "," & ";" by ", " in description
     r←list2,data
⍝ The latest major version of every package, so that the name can lead to its package page.
⍝ Like `uniqueIDs` this relies on the list being in version order, hence the ⌽ again.
     majors←⌽Reg.RemoveMinorAndPatch¨,list
     names←Reg.RemoveVersionNumber¨majors
     r,←majors[names⍳r[;1]]
 :EndIf
